  "executive_briefing": "As of June 2026, the international tax environment is defined by the hardening of the OECD Pillar Two regime and the escalation of trade protectionism via IEEPA-based tariff mandates. The global tax architecture has successfully bifurcated, with the OECD 'side-by-side' agreement cementing a 15% floor for most MNEs while insulating U.S.-headquartered firms. This has prompted a secondary arms race in 'tax competitiveness,' with jurisdictions like Singapore and European nations utilizing tactical rebates and grants to preserve investment appeal. Simultaneously, compliance is undergoing a structural paradigm shift toward real-time transactional transparency, characterized by the mandatory adoption of Peppol-based e-invoicing and digital audit pipelines.",
